Match a config name against the value set of its key

Twenty one readers of a name compare only the head of the text. The name
fullscreen therefore reads as full for focus, flatten reads as flat for
an appearance, and topmost reads as top for tabMouseOver. A name that no
writer stores reaches a live branch, not the default. The three readers
that reach loadValue compare the whole name and take the default, so one
file answers the same question in two ways.

One shared reader serves the four line inputs and accepts dashes for all
four. The writer stores that name for two of them, and the dialog offers
it for the same two. sliderThumbs=dashes paints as dots, leaves the
combination box empty, and turns into sunken on the next save. The shade
reader accepts wborder for every input that accepts darken, although the
dialog holds that entry for the menu bar alone. comboBtn=wborder and
crColor=wborder read as a value that no style path paints and that the
save path rewrites to none.

The reader of an appearance drops a file name of four characters or
fewer. The length test asks for more than nine characters, while the
prefix file: costs five.

Compare each name whole against the names of the key. Take the two gates
from the read site, as the write site takes them. Ask the length test
for one character after the prefix.

The change sits on the branch work/config-io of the local tree, as commit 8 of 18.
A new merge request on system/qtcurve takes that branch.

Drop this patch when upstream merges the change.

